   "text": "I read the structure in four pieces and joined them into one SMILES.\n\n**Left end:** a benzothiophene-2-carboxamide with a CF2\u2013PO3H2 group at C5. The carboxamide N is attached to the bicyclic core.\n\n**Bicyclic core:** an eight-membered ring fused to a pyrrolidine. Going round the eight-membered ring: N(CH2CHF2), CH2, CH(NH-amide), C(=O), the pyrrolidine N, the fusion CH, CH2, CH2, back to the first N. The pyrrolidine carbon next to its N carries the C(=O)NH link to the next residue.\n\n**Peptide chain:** the arginine residue has its guanidine side chain, CCCNC(N)=N. It is followed by a 4-tert-butylphenylalanine residue whose carbonyl forms an amide with a piperazine nitrogen.\n\n**Right end:** the other piperazine N carries a three-carbon chain (CCC) ending in an NH on C4 of a 3-(2,6-dioxopiperidin-3-yl)isoindolin-1-one (the lenalidomide-type ligand). The glutarimide stereocentre is drawn with plain bonds, so it has no stereo label.\n\n**Stereochemistry:** I assigned @/@@ at the five wedged centres from the drawing, treating the implicit H as pointing away from the viewer in each case. These are the amide-bearing carbon of the eight-membered ring, the ring-fusion CH, the pyrrolidine CH, the arginine \u03b1-carbon and the phenylalanine \u03b1-carbon.\n\nSMILES: OP(O)(=O)C(F)(F)c1ccc2sc(cc2c1)C(=O)N[C@H]1CN(CC(F)F)CC[C@H]2CC[C@@H](C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCNC(N)=N)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc3ccc(cc3)C(C)(C)C)C(=O)N3CCN(CC3)CCCNc3cccc4C(=O)N(Cc34)C3CCC(=O)NC3=O)N2C1=O"
